messages:
maya: Quick heads-up — noticed streaming examples in the JS and Python guides are broken after the v2 rollout. The chunks now arrive framed differently and our parsing snippets are producing truncated JSON on slow networks.

jon: ugh, saw a support ticket about this this morning. Can you paste an example of the new framing?

maya: sure — v1 emitted NDJSON (newline-delimited JSON blobs). v2 switched to SSE-like framing where chunks are prefixed with `data:` and separated by a double newline. Example chunk we saw: `data: {"token": "Hel"}\n\ndata: {"token": "lo"}\n\n` — our old splitter (`split(/\n/)`) yields invalid partial JSONs.

sasha: that makes sense. I think our JS example is still using the reader + `split('\n')` approach. We should either show an SSE parser or update to `split(/\r?\n\r?\n/)` and ignore blank lines.

kevin: will this affect replay/capture tooling? We replay streams in the qa harness — might need small change in the infra parser. tagging @eli to confirm.

eli: confirmed — infra captures raw bytes but the QA validation expects whole JSON objects. I'll add tolerant parsing in the harness to accept SSE framing, but docs should teach correct approach.

maya: plan: I will open a docs PR that: 1) updates JS snippet to parse SSE-style chunks robustly, 2) adds a Python example using requests/iter_lines, 3) adds a short migration note under v2 changelog. Need quick reviews from eng-runtime and support.

jon: sounds good. For priority — let's mark it P0 for docs site because broken examples are confusing external users.

maya: drafting the JS snippet now. Rough draft to drop in PR:```js
const res = await fetch('/v2/stream', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(payload) });
const reader = res.body.getReader();
const decoder = new TextDecoder();
let buf = '';
while (true) {
  const { value, done } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  buf += decoder.decode(value, { stream: true });
  // SSE-style: events separated by double CRLF
  const parts = buf.split(/\r?\n\r?\n/);
  buf = parts.pop(); // keep trailing partial
  for (const p of parts) {
    const line = p.trim();
    if (!line) continue;
    // each event may have `data: ` prefix; strip it
    const jsonText = line.replace(/^data:\s*/, '');
    try {
      const obj = JSON.parse(jsonText);
      // handle token / delta
      console.log(obj);
    } catch (e) {
      // skip partial or malformed chunks
    }
  }
}
```

maya: And Python suggestion:```py
with requests.post(url, json=payload, stream=True) as r:
    for raw in r.iter_lines(decode_unicode=True):
        if not raw:
            continue
        # SSE-style line like: 'data: {"token":"Hel"}'
        line = raw.decode('utf-8') if isinstance(raw, bytes) else raw
        if line.startswith('data:'):
            json_text = line[len('data:'):].strip()
            try:
                obj = json.loads(json_text)
                print(obj)
            except ValueError:
                # partial or malformed, skip
                continue
```

kevin: looks good. Add a short note about buffering: "don't attempt to JSON.parse a stream chunk-by-line; accumulate events by double-newline boundaries or use an SSE parser."

maya: good call — will add that. Also adding a short compatibility table in the migration guide: v1=NDJSON vs v2=SSE-like (data: + double newline).

jon: who can review PR? I can review content, sasha can sanity-check the snippets, and eli will confirm infra notes.

maya: thanks — I'll tag you all in the PR. ETA: opening in ~45m.

docs-bot: docs build queued — preview will be available at https://deploy-preview.redwood-inference/docs/streaming-migration (automated).

jon: ping once preview is up and I'll skim for clarity.

maya: will do. one more ask: please check all code blocks under "streaming" section for other language SDKs (ts/py/go). We might need tiny edits in the Go example too.

sasha: I'll run a grep across docs for `split(` and `iter_lines` patterns and open follow-up PRs if I find more.

eli: infra update: QA harness patch merged, CI will pass for replay tests. No infra outage.

maya: perfect. thanks everyone :thumbsup:

jon: thanks maya — appreciate the quick turn.

sasha: thanks :rocket:
